  "findings": [
    {
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "Both clean runs hold identical joint targets for 60 steps (2 seconds), with cube-table contact in every hold sample; this is table-supported retention, not airborne force closure."
    },
    {
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "Step lift loses bilateral contact at step 4; ramp lift at step 7. Both have zero maximum cube lift relative to initial position and no full task success."
    },
    {
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "Ramp reduces large lateral control-point motion, but cube remains on table. Slower lift alone does not solve grasp."
    },
    {
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "Loaded fixed-finger contact is at z=0.01818 m; loaded moving-jaw contact at z=0.03996 m near cube top, with normal Z=0.49549."
    },
    {
      "kind": "inference",
      "confidence": "moderate",
      "text": "Asymmetric side/top-edge contact and uncertain inner-pad frame are a higher-priority investigation than increasing force/friction. Exact cooked-hull mismatch and sole root cause are not yet proved."
    },
    {
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "Exploratory -8 mm height run initially timed out closing; a budget covering the full fine-close joint span made close and hold pass, but lift still lost contact at step 2. Height-only tuning did not solve the issue."
    },
    {
      "kind": "observed",
      "text": "Exploratory retained-posture variant lost contact at lift step 6. It retains a posture-bias reference and one tip-height scalar, not full orientation and not zero posture gain."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One seed and one environment per comparison; not generalization or policy-success evidence.",
    "Exploratory runs are dirty development snapshots; only clean_runs bind the final committed source.",
    "Contact audit samples the last physics substep at 30 Hz, not every 120 Hz contact.",
    "The full sequence never reached transport/release; no claim that physical pick-place or learned penetration exploitation is fixed.",
    "Source commit remains the executable evidence anchor; later documentation commit does not rebind run provenance."
  ],
  "next_required_work": [
    "Establish opposing inner-pad contact frames and verify contact points/normals lie on appropriate cube side interiors, rather than relying only on mesh-tip midpoint.",
    "Then retest table-supported grasp, slow airborne retention, transport, opening/release and retreat under unchanged penetration guards.",
    "Resume revision 3 scratch PPO only after the complete physical feasibility gate passes on a clean source commit. Do not tune friction/force or lower success thresholds to hide the failure."
